{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>There is none like El, Jeshurun.</b> Meaning: there is none like the El of Jeshurun who does this thing for them — namely, He who rides the heavens, meaning He rides upon the heavens for the sake of helping Israel. This is what the verse says ״בְּעֶזְרֶךָ״ — to do battle on your behalf, as it says (Exodus 14:14): ״ה׳ יִלָּחֵם לָכֶם״. And when He comes and does battle for them, all the heavens are His chariot. From this it follows that all the forces of the heavens and their array come to the aid of Israel, for the horse is subordinate to the rider."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:22.561898498Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}